# Figma Implementation

- Final visual design follows Figma specs; do not invent layout, typography, color, or motion when specs are missing.
- Current page shells and minimal CSS are temporary foundations only.
- Map Figma components to existing architecture (`layout`, `content`, `media`, `ui`) rather than replacing data layers.
- Preserve semantic HTML, accessibility landmarks, and content-driven data flow while applying visual polish.
- Font files for Manrope, Switzer, and Tabular belong in `public/fonts/`; configure via `src/fonts/local.ts`.
- Homepage visual work follows Figma Desktop nodes; do not invent alternate layouts when specs exist.
